  "claim_boundary": "This standalone source-checkout acquisition owner is production-disabled. Its public acquisition gate throws before reading options, paths, environment, or filesystem state, and the fixed CLI can only reach that gate. A private reviewed backend retains the frozen Windows PowerShell Desktop 5.1 template and records the exact absolute requested executable, exact requested Audit-only argv, and repository-root cwd passed to spawn(); it is not exported and has no injectable executor. Synthetic artifacts declare the same absolute requested argv but a synthetic executable URI and synthetic_not_realized invocation. The real backend inherits the caller environment, does not attest the realized environment, uses no Job Object, and never claims descendant containment. process_started_at_utc is only a caller-clock lower bound taken immediately before spawn(), not an OS process-creation-time attestation. After child close, bounded stdout and stderr are fsynced, read and hashed from their same still-open wx+ descriptors before descriptor close; the offline validator later reopens and revalidates the exact paths. File-descriptor content fsync before process creation is not a guarantee that Windows directory entries survive power loss: directory_entry_durability_guaranteed remains false. The create-only artifact root must have an existing non-symlink direct parent, but ancestor path components and Windows reparse-point trust are not established. The single-attempt/no-overwrite contract applies only to one caller-selected artifact root. Because artifactRoot is not a scope component, the same deterministic scope can be created at multiple distinct roots; cross_root_duplicate_scope_excluded and scope_global_no_retry_proven remain false. The caller-supplied machine and boot identity hashes are non-authoritative inputs bound into the claim and deterministic scope; this owner does not query or attest live machine identity. The terminal always records an independent stream_capture. Exit 0 or 2 with strict compact Audit v2 stdout and empty stderr is only a capture candidate and alone receives an exact windows-event-log-source-audit-capture-envelope.v1 with capture_authoritative=false; every quarantined outcome has capture_envelope=null. Exit 3 with strict failure v1 stdout and every other process/output combination is quarantined. Timeout, overflow, spawn/kill error, or endpoint drift remains quarantined even when a single kill request is accepted; child.kill() is not descendant containment. Failure output never becomes a source-config projection or qualification input. Pre/post source and executable endpoint equality does not prove continuous stability, trusted execution, replay exclusion, or process origin. The public offline validator and declarative synthetic writer establish only artifact self-consistency. All real observation, qualification eligibility or authorization, CUDA, formal evidence, production ACTIVE, Appendable, Readable, Learnable, Steerable, four-capability, tamper-resistance, path-parent trust, and directory-entry durability claims remain false. The bound host-qualification protocol remains unchanged and does not automatically consume this artifact."
